M11 Sydney rally legs retry a failed path a bounded number of times.
The rally legs WAYPATH_01..04 (cell to rally zone 01, 02, 03a/03b) leave
sydneys_location at IDLE, so the PATH_BAD_START, PATH_BAD_DEST and
MOVE_NO_PROGRESS_MADE branches, which only re-send the elevator and switch
stages, ignore them. A failed rally-leg solve left Sydney standing, and the
rally zone she would arm never fired.

Record each rally leg's action id and waypath (start/end) where it is issued.
On one of those failures, while she is still IDLE and alive, re-issue the same
goto (same waypath, priority and speed) 2 s later, at most 3 times per leg,
with a log breadcrumb for each retry and for the limit. The timer id is the
leg's action id, so a pending retry for a leg that has been replaced does
nothing. State is saved on unused ids 15-19. A leg that succeeds is unchanged.

